    {
      "id": "7d39cd26-310b-487e-9a1d-632c73360c51",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        608,
        10080
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 960,
        "content": "## Monitor Wayfair product prices with Apify and alert on new lows via Gmail\n\n### Who's it for\n\nDeal-hunters and e-commerce teams who want to track Wayfair prices around the clock, keep a historical record, and get an email the moment a product hits a new low. It replaces manual price checks with a scheduled workflow you set up once.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs every six hours to scrape a Wayfair product with Apify, then records the current price in Google Sheets. It reads the accumulated price history, computes the lowest recorded price, and checks whether the latest snapshot is a new low. If it is, the workflow sends a Gmail alert.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger interval if six hours is not desired.\n- Connect Apify credentials and configure the actor/task with the target Wayfair product URL and output fields needed for price tracking.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the spreadsheet/sheet used to append snapshots and read historical prices.\n- Ensure the sheet has consistent columns for timestamp, product identifier/name, and price so the code node can compute the minimum correctly.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and set the alert recipient, subject, and message body.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can change the tracked product, alert threshold logic, price-history sheet structure, or notification destination to fit different products and monitoring rules.\nSwap Gmail for Slack, Discord, or a webhook to change the alert channel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ab324f65-e268-440a-bb23-746f0257e62a",
